  What:the policy,desc:how this map is kept — each rule is one What below with the rule as its desc
    What:one Waft per area,desc:a ghost lives in ONE area Waft — a Doc may be cited from another area only under a What that says why
    What:Points are the main functions,desc:a Point method is an entry the reader should know — with keywords as its desc — not every def — the code is the full list
    What:no commas in a desc,desc:the peel parser splits on commas — use an em-dash
    What:Books live in CreduFunk,desc:an area Waft lists its FIXTURED Books under Funkcion:CreduFunk so they run from there — Credence stays the full index
    What:the spec What is last,desc:specs and todos sit under What:the spec at the tail — a _todo opens with §0 what to get on with next — only the human promotes a doc to _spec
    What:rebalance when an area splits,desc:when a Waft passes about 150 lines or two stories live in it — split it and add the new Waft here
    What:stale names are bugs,desc:a Doc path or Point that no longer resolves is a mint bug — scripts/wafts_everything.mjs validates every one before writing — re-run it after a rename
    What:new sessions read this Waft first,desc:then the area Waft for the work at hand — then its _todo §0
